/-!
# Linear series on a smooth proper curve in characteristic `p`

Let `k` be a field of characteristic `p > 0`, let `X` be a smooth proper curve over `k` and let
`(ℒ, V)` be a `𝔤^r_d` on `X`, [Stacks, Tag 0CCN], with `r ≥ 1`. This file proves
[Stacks, Tag 0CD3]: either some `𝔤¹_d` on `X` has a generically etale morphism to `ℙ¹_k`, or the
Frobenius twist `X^{(p)}` of [Stacks, Tag 0CC9] carries a `𝔤^r_{d'}` with `d' ≤ d / p`.

Which alternative holds is decided by the ratios `f_j = s_j / s_0` of a basis `s_0, …, s_r` of
`V`, read at the generic point of `X` as elements of the function field `k(X)`. The compositum of
`k` with the `p`-th powers of `k(X)` is the image of `k(X^{(p)})`, by [Stacks, Tag 07P2] at the
generic point. If every `f_j` lies in it, the morphism `φ_{(ℒ', (s_0, …, s_r))} : X ⟶ ℙ^r_k` of
[Stacks, Tag 01ND] attached to the subsheaf `ℒ' ⊆ ℒ` generated by the basis factors through the
relative Frobenius, by [Stacks, Tag 0BXZ]; the factoring morphism pulls `𝒪(1)` back to an
invertible sheaf on `X^{(p)}` with `r + 1` independent sections and degree `d'` satisfying
`p · d' = deg ℒ' ≤ d`, the last inequality being [Stacks, Tag 0B40] part (5). If some `f_j`
escapes it, the pencil spanned by `s_0` and `s_j` is a `𝔤¹_d` whose morphism to `ℙ¹_k` is
dominant with a finite separable extension of function fields, which is the fifth condition of
the [Stacks, Tag 0C1C] list and hence generic etaleness.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.exists_genericallyEtale_pencil_or_linearSeries_frobeniusTwist`:
  **[Stacks, Tag 0CD3]**, the whole disjunction at the source's hypotheses.

## Implementation notes

"The corresponding morphism of [Stacks, Tag 0CCP]" is pinned by carrying the data that tag
produces: the first alternative provides not only a `𝔤¹_d` `E₁` and a morphism
`q : X ⟶ ℙ¹_k` over `k`, but a basis `b₁` of the pencil's space of sections and a map
`α : q^* 𝒪(1) ⟶ E₁.L` sending the pulled-back homogeneous coordinate `q^* T_i` to the section
underlying `b₁ i`. That pinning is exactly the conclusion of
`Stacks.LinearSeriesMorphism.exists_hom_over_and_hom_pullback_twistingSheafAtUniverse_of_basis`,
so `q` is the morphism of Tag 0CCP for `(E₁, b₁)` rather than an unrelated morphism of the same
shape; `α` is built here from the pinned twist comparison of [Stacks, Tag 01NE] at the canonical
morphism, `AlgebraicGeometry.exists_iso_twistingSheafAtUniverse_toProjectiveSpaceAtUniverse`,
followed by the inclusion of the subsheaf generated by the pencil's two sections.

"Generically etale" is rendered as clause (4) of the [Stacks, Tag 0C1C] list,
`∃ U : X.Opens, Nonempty U ∧ Etale (U.ι ≫ q)`: etale on a nonempty open. The proof produces
clause (5) — dominance together with a finite separable extension of residue fields at the
generic point — and moves to clause (4) along `AlgebraicGeometry.genericallyEtale_tfae`.

The Frobenius twist of [Stacks, Tag 0CC9] is `X^{(p)}`, here the base change
`AlgebraicGeometry.frobeniusTwist` of `X` along the absolute Frobenius of `Spec k`; it is a
smooth proper curve over `k` by the results of
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Curves.FrobeniusTwistCurve`, which is what lets it carry a
linear series at all.

Both readings of `d' ≤ d / p` are given: the natural-number division `d' ≤ d / p` as the source
writes it, and the integral form `p * d' ≤ d` which is the inequality the proof establishes and
the one a consumer can use without a divisibility side condition.

The source's `r ≥ 1` is kept as the source states it, as the hypothesis `_hr`.

Two spellings of the function field are in play and the transport between them is where most of
the work sits. The ratios, `AlgebraicGeometry.functionFieldMap` and `compositumFrobenius` live on
`X.functionField`, the stalk at the generic point; clause (5) of Tag 0C1C and
`AlgebraicGeometry.fieldRange_residueFieldMap_relativeFrobenius` live on
`X.residueField (genericPoint X)`. `genericResidueAlgEquiv` upgrades
`AlgebraicGeometry.genericResidueEquiv` to a `k`-algebra equivalence between the two, which moves
the compositum across, and
`AlgebraicGeometry.residueFieldMap_comp_genericResidueEquivOfDominant` moves finiteness and
separability across.

## References

